{{define "estates"}}
<h1>Estates</h1>

<p>Real configurations taken through the crossing pipeline against a local AWS
emulator. Each one stands up from nothing, adopts its markers, loses its state
file, and is replanned. Where an estate stopped is where the work is.</p>

<h2>The stages</h2>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>What it proves</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>stands up from nothing</td><td>A cold apply creates the estate.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>adopts its markers</td><td>Ownership tags land on every resource.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>replans empty, no state file</td><td>The state file is deleted and the plan is still empty. This is the claim.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>applies again cleanly</td><td>A second apply adds nothing.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>drifts and reconverges</td><td>Drift is introduced out of band, detected, and corrected.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Every estate</h2>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Estate</th><th>Reached</th><th>Lane</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {{range .Estates}}<tr>
    <td><code>{{.Name}}</code></td>
    <td{{if .Complete}} class="estate-complete"{{end}}>{{.Reached}}</td>
    <td>{{.Lane}}</td>
  </tr>{{end}}
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>What each one is</h2>

<dl class="estate-sources">
{{range .Estates}}
  <dt><code>{{.Name}}</code></dt>
  <dd>{{.Source}}</dd>
{{end}}
</dl>

<p>Each estate lives at its directory in the repository with a
<code>run.sh</code> beside it. The exit code is the verdict. Rendered from
<code>live/corpus-crossing-manifest.json</code>.</p>
{{end}}
